          "after": [
            "⚠️ **Note the recurring pattern: every *o* and *u* sound gets an extra ו, every *i* sound gets a י.** שֻׁלְחָן becomes שולחן; שֵׁרוּתִים becomes שירותים. The rest you guess from words you already know — and you know more than three hundred words by now.",
            "Reassuring news: **you guess far less than you think.** Hebrew words grow from three-letter roots with a limited set of vowel patterns, so once you see כתב you know there are only a handful of options. It's just like reading \"txt msg\" in English and instantly knowing it's \"text message\"."
