          "type": "kotak",
          "title": "Asking the way",
          "items": [
            "**סְלִיחָה, אֵיפֹה ...?** — excuse me, where is ...?",
            "**אֵיךְ מַגִּיעִים לְ...?** *(eikh magi'im le...?)* — how do I get to...? Literally \"how do they arrive to\" — a subjectless form Israelis use all the time.",
            "**זֶה רָחוֹק מִכָּאן?** — is it far from here?",
            "**אֶפְשָׁר לָלֶכֶת בְּרֶגֶל?** — can I walk there?",
            "**אֲנִי הָלַכְתִּי לְאִבּוּד** *(ani halakhti le'ibud)* — I'm lost. A sentence you hopefully won't need, but better to have."
          ]
        }
      ]
